/farmland-atlas/kansas/cheyenne-county"],["ARC or PLC in Cheyenne County","/arc-plc/kansas/cheyenne-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids February to March came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those years. So far in 2026, the county&rsquo;s middle value got 25% of normal in January to February and 14% of normal in February to March. May to June is the wettest pair at 5.82 inches of normal. Grid 23512 had its driest year in 1954 at 46% of normal.</p>"}
